Since you already know:

* ✅ ANN
* ✅ CNN
* ✅ Deep Learning fundamentals
* ✅ NLP (finishing this week)

you're at a good point to move into **LLMs and Generative AI**. If your goal is to become **job-ready** for roles like **AI Engineer, LLM Engineer, or GenAI Engineer**, don't focus only on prompt engineering. Companies expect you to know how to build and deploy LLM applications.

## Skills you should learn next (in order)

### Phase 1: Transformers and LLM Fundamentals (1–2 weeks)

Understand:

* Attention mechanism
* Self-attention
* Positional encoding
* Encoder vs Decoder
* BERT
* GPT
* T5
* Llama
* Mixture of Experts (MoE)

Recommended course:

* [DeepLearning.AI – Generative AI with LLMs](https://www.deeplearning.ai/courses/generative-ai-with-llms/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

